n doesn't accept a copy keyword, so passing copy=False failed. __array__ must implement 'dtype' and 'copy' keyword arguments. To learn more, see the migration guide https://numpy.org/devdocs/numpy_2_0_migration_guide.html#adapting-to-changes-in-the-copy-keyword\nTotal couch pixels in F1: 4164\ny range: 271 332 x range: 104 217"},"7f0e0ef07dcbb69c5f583a575bb539a2ddd99c95f6ebc0d369d83fe7270569bb":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ten consecutive columns all show a constant y-value of about -0.64, indicating the south wall sits there rather than at -1.30 as previously recorded. But that conflicts with obs_0005, which was fully white when facing south — if the wall were really at y=-0.64, the floor junction should have appeared at a specific pixel row, so I need to reconcile this discrepancy.\n\nActually working through the math, the junction row exceeds the image bounds, so all-white is exactly what's expected at that distance and camera height — this confirms south wall y = -0.64. That gives room dimensions of x from -3.93 to 3.93 and y from -0.64 to 8.27.\n\nNow I need to dead-reckon the heading through frames 102-104: starting around h=225 at f102, then +90 and +45 turns bring me to h=0, facing north at f104, which should let me pin down the north wall position at y=8.27. Let me record these findings in notes first, then analyze the obs_0104 images.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Ten consecutive columns hold y = **-0.64** — that's the south wall, measured at zero drift from the origin. It also explains why obs_0005 was pure white: a wall 0.64 m away puts its floor junction at v≈876, far below the frame. The old stored value of -1.30 was wrong."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SMC4ck8mkPkKr5ehwGLheP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> notes.md <<'EOF'\n\n## ROOM BOUNDS CORRECTED (frames 1-8, camera EXACTLY at origin => zero drift, no pose error)\nSUPERSEDES old W=-3.30 / E=3.68 / N=8.25 / S=-1.30. All below are absolute measurements.\n  NORTH  y = +8.27   (obs_0001, 9-sample constant-v=304 run u128..336)\n  EAST   x = +3.93   (obs_0003 h=90, 12 exact samples)\n  WEST   x = -3.93   (obs_0007 h=270, 8 exact samples; obs_0001 gave -3.95)\n  SOUTH  y = -0.64   (obs_0007 h=270, 10 consecutive columns u154..214 all y=-0.64/-0.65)\n  => room 7.86 m (x) x 8.91 m (y). Start sits only 0.64 m off the south wall.\n  Cross-check: obs_0005 (h=180, faces S) is ALL WHITE. Wall at 0.64m => junction v=876 >511. CONSISTENT.\n  obs_0004/obs_0006 diagonal fits (perp~0.96 rms~0.085) are CONTAMINATED - ignore them.\nBONUS zero-drift confirmation: obs_0007 u384/u416 -> (-2.48,1.24), (-2.42,1.51) = blue_vase_1. Matches stored (-2.46,1.45).\nEOF\necho written\npython3 -c \"\nfrom PIL import Image\nimport numpy as np, math\nfor f in ['obs_0103','obs_0104']:\n    im=np.array(Image.open('/work/observations/%s.png'%f).convert('RGB')).astype(int)\n    R,G,B=im[:,:,0],im[:,:,1],im[:,:,2]\n    fl=(abs(R-G)<25)&(R>120)&(R<190)&(G>110)&(B>90)&(B<165)&(R-B>15)\n    print('===',f,'floor px',fl.sum())\n    for u in range(0,512,48):\n        c=np.nonzero(fl[:,u])[0]\n        print('  u%3d'%u, 'none' if not len(c) else 'top v=%d bot v=%d'%(c.min(),c.max()))\n\" 2>/dev/null"}}]},"7fa2edda466f81f9146bfa334cb690eb64c51691d9173764a6259a4488a188bc":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Turning 90 degrees to heading 270 and moving 0.75 units, the position shifts left to (1.450, 7.400). Now I want to check this against the image.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EJCtdrBugotrEiwiascuS7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/work/observations/obs_0153.png"}}]},"7f8f6b0646f4f8cd3304f54b162199173888f6c6acdf8a279a1cb2f6488a0479":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool result metadata: {\"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_012h4K8Z37DtHFJ1i3u25HAn\", \"type\": \"tool_result\", \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}"},{"type":"image_url","image_url":{"url":"/media/460128257c269e3f